								I&#039;m a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=303"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16783#msg16783"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16783#msg16783">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2838 on:</b> May 03, 2005, 09:10:53 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">And the UoP I joined and am currently in has not used this type of tactic at any time that I&#039;m aware of </div><br />Then you asked for an example. Well here it is.<br /><br />Ask any ex-hegemony member about UoP cock-blocking Emp in Ssra for months, keeping hegemony out of VT. Then when we go to do VT (clearing from zone in, already in zone), UOP (more experienced and better at knowing the safe spots), jumps ahead of us the 2 times we go after it.<br /><br />So we abandoned VT and went strickly with PoP content. Why? because UoP were being asses. plain and simple.<br /><br />I have no clue if this is still the philosophy of the guild. I have no clue if the officers are the same. I certainly don&#039;t bring it up to the UoP people I grind with on occasion. As Ted Kennedy would say: &quot;It&#039;s water under the bridge&quot;.<br /><br />but...don&#039;t come here and act like UoP is squeeky clean.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
