	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg16789"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371" title="View the profile of Shakro">Shakro</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 145<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/coolbear.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								<a href="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/about_me/1,,,00.html?Uin=24026767" target="_blank"><img src="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/online?icq=24026767&amp;img=5" alt="24026767" width="18" height="18" border="0" /></a>
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16789#msg16789"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16789#msg16789">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2842 on:</b> May 03, 2005, 10:22:52 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I can&#039;t believe UoP members don&#039;t know their guild&#039;s own history.&nbsp; True, you guys posting are probably newer, and were in different guilds back then, but RN is an old server, and guild reputations tend to linger perhaps longer than is deserved.<br /><br />What I don&#039;t understand is, why does UoP need the fish again?&nbsp; Surely you have everyone FR, Xeg, TRC flagged by now.&nbsp; That means that entire force you used to kill Coirnav the first time is surely now time flagged.&nbsp; Should be at least 55 people or so, right?&nbsp; That&#039;s plenty to begin farming time with, considering you can 83/17 another 10 to 12 and then begin to backflag them all with the key that drops in time.&nbsp; Seems alot easier to do imo, unless you had alot of people leave the guild after that Coir kill... but it&#039;s your decision what mobs you go after.&nbsp; I wish yall luck with the spawn and the kill.<br /><br />As for OA... OA is certainly entitled to kill or attempt any mob they want.&nbsp; I understand yall have gotten close on Coirnav.&nbsp; Just realize that choosing to attempt a mob multiple times that&#039;s standing between 2 other guilds and Time won&#039;t win you friends with those guilds, and it&#039;s probably already built up animosity.&nbsp; It&#039;s your right, but realize that Coirnav is the only contested progression mob in the elemental planes.&nbsp; IL didn&#039;t want any other target, I know they logged some nights because that one target wasn&#039;t up.&nbsp; UoP probably doesn&#039;t want the other elemental targets.&nbsp; It seems like you have unintentionally cockblocked some guilds from being able to move on to Time, when you guys are still a ways away from that zone yourselves.&nbsp; OA are nice people, I don&#039;t know why you&#039;d choose to get into that contest when it doesn&#039;t set you back to concentrate on, let&#039;s say, winning the Dust Ring in Air?&nbsp; Again tho, your right, raid where you choose.<br /><br />Just like it didn&#039;t violate any rules that I know of for IL to kill the Coir trigger.&nbsp; They needed the mob, and lacked the time zone advantage to kill it.&nbsp; &quot;You should raid earlier&quot; is a lame comeback when the guild can only raid late at night due to time zone differences.&nbsp; I don&#039;t think it&#039;s the nicest thing to do, but I understand why they did it.&nbsp; I would feel differently if they were killing the trigger to prevent someone&#039;s progression, but they did it in order to progress themselves.&nbsp; Kudos.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><img src="http://i3.photobucket.com/albums/y68/tvsbill/6fbdd1b6.jpg" alt="" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
