							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16789#msg16789">Quote from: Shakro on May 03, 2005, 10:22:52 am</a></div><div class="quote">I can&#039;t believe UoP members don&#039;t know their guild&#039;s own history.  True, you guys posting are probably newer, and were in different guilds back then, but RN is an old server, and guild reputations tend to linger perhaps longer than is deserved.<br /><br />What I don&#039;t understand is, why does UoP need the fish again?  Surely you have everyone FR, Xeg, TRC flagged by now.  That means that entire force you used to kill Coirnav the first time is surely now time flagged.  Should be at least 55 people or so, right?  That&#039;s plenty to begin farming time with, considering you can 83/17 another 10 to 12 and then begin to backflag them all with the key that drops in time.  Seems alot easier to do imo, unless you had alot of people leave the guild after that Coir kill... but it&#039;s your decision what mobs you go after.  I wish yall luck with the spawn and the kill.<br /><br />As for OA... OA is certainly entitled to kill or attempt any mob they want.  I understand yall have gotten close on Coirnav.  Just realize that choosing to attempt a mob multiple times that&#039;s standing between 2 other guilds and Time won&#039;t win you friends with those guilds, and it&#039;s probably already built up animosity.  It&#039;s your right, but realize that Coirnav is the only contested progression mob in the elemental planes.  IL didn&#039;t want any other target, I know they logged some nights because that one target wasn&#039;t up.  UoP probably doesn&#039;t want the other elemental targets.  It seems like you have unintentionally cockblocked some guilds from being able to move on to Time, when you guys are still a ways away from that zone yourselves.  OA are nice people, I don&#039;t know why you&#039;d choose to get into that contest when it doesn&#039;t set you back to concentrate on, let&#039;s say, winning the Dust Ring in Air?  Again tho, your right, raid where you choose.<br /><br />Just like it didn&#039;t violate any rules that I know of for IL to kill the Coir trigger.  They needed the mob, and lacked the time zone advantage to kill it.  &quot;You should raid earlier&quot; is a lame comeback when the guild can only raid late at night due to time zone differences.  I don&#039;t think it&#039;s the nicest thing to do, but I understand why they did it.  I would feel differently if they were killing the trigger to prevent someone&#039;s progression, but they did it in order to progress themselves.  Kudos.<br /></div><br />OA has done the dust ring and we have access to xegony.  We are 3 kills away and thats not far off just ask DN how long it took to get from 3 kills away to what time being beaten.  That was what like 3 weeks or so if that.  Don&#039;t try and play the you shouldn&#039;t get envoled by tring coirnav becuase you might make people mad. <br /><br />&nbsp;I could care less if UoP is pissed off and IL isn&#039;t even on our raid time so it doesn&#039;t matter.  What matters is our progression not who is close to what.  Hell I wouldn&#039;t be shocked if the next time we attempt Coirnav the fish goes down.  Xegony will be down pretty soon.&nbsp; That would leave us with 1 event left.  You make it sound like the events are hard.&nbsp; Its still tough but most guilds are taking, what,&nbsp; between 2 to 5 attemps before knocking them out ?<br /><br />  If UoP doesn&#039;t want to take out other targets that there own fualts for passing up loot for there members.  That should show you how dumb leadership is that you would call a raid becuase the one target isnt up when you can do others and get good loot for your members.  
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: May 03, 2005, 10:55:55 am by Carsonn</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
